README.md:99:- **`--logs`** — Streams app logs from the simulator or emulator, prefixed with `[log]` and interleaved with the flow output. On iOS (`xcrun simctl spawn log stream`) the predicate is scoped to your app: subsystems starting with its bundle ID, plus every line from its process (the installed app's `CFBundleExecutable`); override it with `--logs-predicate`. On Android `logcat` is filtered to the app's uid; `--logs-tag <tag>` keeps one tag and implies `--logs`. `--logs-level default|info|debug` sets the level on both (see [docs/android.md](docs/android.md#logs)).
README.md:197:| `GRANTIVA_DRIVER_START_TIMEOUT` | Seconds the runner waits for the UIAutomator2 server to start on Android (the runner's default is 30). Raise it on a slow or busy host; `runner start` then waits for the session for twice this plus 30 seconds (at least 90). A start that fails says so at once, with the runner's reason. |
